{"query":"Sleeping under a mosquito bed net treated (or not treated) with insecticide is ineffective and harmful to human health. original source fact check","results":[{"date":"Apr 2, 2024","position":1,"site_name":"www.cdc.gov","snippet":"The insecticides used on ITNs have been shown to pose very low health risks to humans and other mammals but are toxic to insects and kill them.","title":"Insecticide-Treated Nets | Malaria","url":"https://www.cdc.gov/malaria/php/public-health-strategy/insecticide-treated-nets.html"},{"date":"Apr 25, 2017","position":2,"site_name":"www.afro.who.int","snippet":"WHO recommends that all people at risk of malaria sleep under ITNs particularly long lasting insecticidal nets (LLINs) every night","title":"Treated mosquito nets are safe and effective | WHO","url":"https://www.afro.who.int/news/treated-mosquito-nets-are-safe-and-effective"},{"position":3,"site_name":"www.facebook.com","snippet":"MYTH: Insecticide-treated bed nets (ITNs) do not work and are harmful to humans. FACT: When properly used, ITNs reduce the risk of malaria.","title":"MYTH: Insecticide-treated bed nets (ITNs) do not work and are harmful to ...","url":"https://www.facebook.com/U.S.EmbassyNairobi/videos/myth-insecticide-treated-bed-nets-itns-do-not-work-and-are-harmful-to-humansfact/2210387322385012/"},{"position":4,"site_name":"link.springer.com","snippet":"by AR Akello · 2022 · Cited by 57 — The use of insecticide-treated bed nets has been proven to be effective in reducing malaria transmission in highly endemic areas.","title":"Factors influencing consistent use of bed nets for the control of malaria ...","url":"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12936-022-04396-z"},{"position":5,"site_name":"pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov","snippet":"by NG Onyeneho · 2013 · Cited by 25 — Health education would dispel misconceptions that ITNs could kill, curtail human fertility, and that local gin (Kai-Kai) would induce sleep and make one ...","title":"Sleeping under Insecticide-treated Nets to Prevent Malaria in Nigeria","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3702346/"},{"position":6,"site_name":"www.cdcfoundation.org","snippet":"An insecticide-treated bed net protects the person sleeping under the net even if the net has small holes in it, because the insecticide kills mosquitoes","title":"Bed Nets for Children","url":"https://www.cdcfoundation.org/bednets"},{"date":"Jul 27, 2026","position":7,"site_name":"ourworldindata.org","snippet":"The share of children under five years old who slept under an insecticide-treated bednet to prevent malaria infection the previous night.","title":"Share of children sleeping under insecticide-treated nets, 2021","url":"https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/children-sleeping-under-treated-bednet"},{"position":8,"site_name":"www.givewell.org","snippet":"We estimate that sleeping under nets reduces malaria mortality by around 40% to 55% in locations where GiveWell fund campaigns.","title":"Mass Distribution of Insecticide-Treated Nets (ITNs)","url":"https://www.givewell.org/international/technical/programs/insecticide-treated-nets"},{"position":9,"site_name":"en.wikipedia.org","snippet":"Research has shown mosquito nets to be an extremely effective method of malaria prevention. A 2025 analysis by the Malaria Atlas Project reported that ...","title":"Mosquito net","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mosquito_net"},{"date":"Oct 22, 2024","position":10,"site_name":"effectivealtruism.nz","snippet":"Insecticide-treated bednets are one of the most effective tools for combating malaria: a disease that still claims hundreds of thousands of ...","title":"Should we be worried about mosquito net fishing?","url":"https://effectivealtruism.nz/blog/should-we-worry-about-bednet-fishing"}],"total_results":10,"page":0}